WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.176 --> 00:00:11.545
Operator dashboard: the conversation arrives with a response timer and the customer’s language.

2
00:00:11.645 --> 00:00:16.942
The operator writes the reply and sends it. Nothing is sent automatically.

3
00:00:17.042 --> 00:00:22.388
Live queue: available operators, queue size and active conversations refresh automatically.

4
00:00:22.488 --> 00:00:27.791
Every conversation is listed with its state, language and the operator who holds it.

5
00:00:27.891 --> 00:00:37.965
Escalation: an operator who needs a decision escalates to a supervisor with a note.

6
00:00:38.065 --> 00:00:44.109
Supervisor dashboard: the escalation appears in the supervisor queue and the supervisor takes it.

7
00:00:44.209 --> 00:00:55.174
Quality control: supervisors score sent replies on accuracy, tone and resolution, with a coaching note.

8
00:00:55.274 --> 00:01:02.535
Multilingual operations: conversations are routed only to operators who handle the customer’s language, and gaps are flagged.

9
00:01:02.635 --> 00:01:11.015
Adding a language to an operator updates coverage straight away.

10
00:01:11.115 --> 00:01:18.300
The complete workflow: message in, assigned, answered by a human operator, and kept on record for supervisors.

